<p class="nest-overview-tagline">Tools for hatching new Flutters</p>

<section id="what-is-it">
    <p><span class="emphasis">Nest</span>  •  Nest is a collection of scripts, extensions, and
      education designed to help anyone create and maintain a Flutter fork. Nest is the tooling that makes Flock possible.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="patches">
    <h2>Patches</h2>
    <p>Nest-based forks are fundamentally based on patches. A Flutter fork, which uses Nest, takes the entire commit history of Flutter, and then puts some set of patches on top. This is what makes the fork maintainable.</p>
    <p>Nest includes its own patch file protocol. This protocol is nearly identical to the standard <em>git email patch format</em>, with a few extensions for Nest use-cases.</p>
    <p>Read more about <a href="/nest/patches/">patches</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="githubWorkflows">
    <h2>GitHub Workflows</h2>
    <p>Nest provides GitHub workflows to help automate maintenance of Flutter forks.</p>
    <p>Read more about <a href="/nest/github-workflows/">GitHub workflows</a></p>
  </section>